==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/t͡sɪmt/|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From late {{inh|de|gmh|zimet}} (whence also archaic {{m|de|Zimmet}}), from {{inh|de|gmh|zinemīn}}, {{m|gmh|zinment}}, from {{der|de|la|cinnamon}}, {{m|la|cinnamomum}}, from {{der|de|grc|κίνναμον}}, {{m|grc|κινναμωμον}}, from {{der|de|phn}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Zimts|gen2=Zimtes|-}}

# [[cinnamon]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|de|Zimtschnecke}}
* {{l|de|Zimtaldehyd}}
* {{l|de|Zimtbaum}}
* {{l|de|Zimtöl}}
* {{l|de|Zimtstange}}

===Etymology 2===
From the adjective {{m|de|zimt}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|n|Zimts|-}}

# the brownish colour of [[cinnamon]]

===Etymology 3===
From [[w:Rotwelsch|Rotwelsch]] {{m|de|Zimt||gold}}<!--, as in "Mach kein Gold", "Don't fake any gold"-->.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Zimts|gen2=Zimtes|Zimte}}

# something worthless or dumb

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|de|Zimtzicke}}

